  "query_preview": ".. (Thursday Night through Next Wednesday)\n\nA strong Canadian high tracking from Manitoba (Thursday) to \nQuebec (Saturday) will initially push the surface boundary south\nacross central Illinois before southerly return flow nudges it \nback northward late in the week. The persisting frontal boundary\nover the region will maintain daily precipitation chances \nalongside a sharp north-to-south temperature contrast (mid 90s \nsouth, low 80s north). Strong diurnal destabilization combined \nwith modest deep-layer shear will keep a low-end threat for a\nfew stronger storms in place Thursday and Friday.\n\nA broader synoptic pattern change arrives late weekend as the \nupper-level ridge centered over the southern/southeastern CONUS \nbreaks down. An upper low tracking across the northern Great \nPlains into the Upper Midwest will sweep another round of \nshowers and thunderstorms through the region on Sunday. Cooler \nair filtering in behind this system will finally push 90-degree \ntemperatures south of the area through the first half of next \nweek while precip chances gradually become more muted in the\ndrier air mass..",
